.TH HD-BACKUP-VMS 8 "October 2026" "hd-backup" "HyprDebian"
.SH NAME
hd-backup-vms \- back up the virtual machines in the configuration
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B hd-backup-vms
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B hd-backup-vms
backs up every virtual machine in the key
.B hd-backup
of
.IR /etc/hyprdebian/config.json ,
one after the other, with
.BR hd\-backup\-vm (8).
A VM whose backup fails does not stop the backups of the others; the command
fails at the end when one failed, or when an entry is invalid.
Run it as root.
.PP
.B hd-backup-vms.timer
runs it through
.B hd-backup-vms.service
every night at 3:30; a run that was missed while the system was off runs at
the next boot.
The package does not enable the timer.
Enable it with:
.PP
.RS
sudo systemctl enable \-\-now hd-backup-vms.timer
.RE
.PP
The output of the backups is in the journal:
.PP
.RS
journalctl \-u hd-backup-vms.service
.RE
.SH SETTINGS
The key
.B hd-backup
of
.IR /etc/hyprdebian/config.json ,
see
.BR hd\-config (7),
holds a JSON array with an object per VM, with the arguments of
.BR hd\-backup\-vm :
.TP
.B vm
The name of the VM in libvirt.
.TP
.B dir
The folder that holds the backup folder of the VM; the backup goes to
.IR dir / vm .
.TP
.B owner
The user who gets the files of the backup.
.PP
The installation stores an empty array when the key is missing.
For example:
.PP
.RS
.nf
sudo hd-config-update hd-backup \e
    '[{"vm": "git", "dir": "/dpool/backups/vm", "owner": "erik"}]'
.fi
.RE
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 when every backup finished, also when there are none; 1 on an error.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/hyprdebian/config.json
The VMs to back up, in the key
.BR hd-backup .
.TP
.I /usr/lib/systemd/system/hd-backup-vms.timer
.TQ
.I /usr/lib/systemd/system/hd-backup-vms.service
Run hd-backup-vms every night at 3:30.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR hd\-backup\-vm (8),
.BR hd\-restore\-vm (8),
.BR hd\-config\-update (8)
